WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.392
Quantization lowers the numerical precision used for model weights and sometimes other data.

00:00:05.392 --> 00:00:07.835
It reduces memory and bandwidth pressure,

00:00:07.835 --> 00:00:12.720
making local inference practical on hardware that cannot support the original precision.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.826
The savings can improve model loading and allow more layers to remain on an accelerator,

00:00:18.826 --> 00:00:23.711
but scales, metadata, activations, runtime buffers, and context cache still consume memory.

00:00:23.711 --> 00:00:26.561
Precision labels describe tradeoffs, not guaranteed outcomes.

00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:31.039
FP16, BF16, INT8, and low-bit formats require compatible hardware and runtimes.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:34.703
GGUF and safetensors are containers used in different workflows;

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:37.553
neither extension alone establishes quality or precision.

00:00:37.553 --> 00:00:41.624
Tokenizers, templates, architecture metadata, and model revisions must remain compatible.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:44.066
Q4 is often a useful baseline,

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:48.137
while lower levels favor fit and higher levels favor fidelity.

00:00:48.137 --> 00:00:53.836
The right choice depends on model architecture, available VRAM or RAM, context, batch, offload,

00:00:53.836 --> 00:00:55.872
kernel support, and task sensitivity.

00:00:55.872 --> 00:01:00.757
A model that barely fits may run worse than a smaller or

00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:02.792
more compact option with headroom.

00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:04.014
Choose through testing.

00:01:04.014 --> 00:01:08.492
Compare several variants with the same runtime, prompts, settings, and hardware.

00:01:08.492 --> 00:01:12.970
Measure speed and memory, evaluate factual and task quality, repeat trials,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.598
and record the configuration.

00:01:14.598 --> 00:01:20.297
Quantization succeeds when it preserves the quality required by the workload while delivering stable,

00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:22.740
maintainable performance on the target system.
